 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Pass of Sirion"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/place
  :entry/description "The Pass of Sirion, in the _First Age_, was a steep-sided pass between the _Ered Wethrin_ and the _Echoriath_, on the upper reaches of the River _Sirion_. The only road through the pass was narrow and ran along the western bank of the river. The sheer walls were covered with pines yet the vale was green. In the middle of the pass was the isle of _Tol Sirion_ where _Finrod_ built the tower of Minas Tirith. After _Finrod_ departed to _Nargothrond_ the fortress was committed to _Finrod_’s kinsman _Orodreth_."
  :entry/page       [105 110 143 151 168 182 184 201 205]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Of the Return of the Noldor"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Beleriand and its Realms"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Ruin of Beleriand and the Fall of Fingolfin"]
