 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Vale of Sirion"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/place
  :entry/description "The Vale(s) of Sirion was the wide valley of the River _Sirion_, that separated West _Beleriand_ from East _Beleriand_. The term seems to apply especially to that part of the river’s course around the _Pass of Sirion_ that lay to the north of _Doriath_. These waters were protected by _Ulmo_ until some point prior to F.A. 495; at that time, two messengers from _Círdan_ bore tidings to _Orodreth_ that the Evil of the North had defiled the springs of _Sirion_, and _Ulmo_’s power had withdrawn."
  :entry/page       [43 97 105 109 117 192 205 233]
